<title>HONG KONG: DC Finance 1996 profit jumps sharply.</title>
<headline>DC Finance 1996 profit jumps sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   36.7	  vs 4.2 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    4.5	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  113.09 gain vs 21.23 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    188.07	vs 20.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		     264.08	vs 14.47</p>
<p>    Company name		 DC Finance (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 3-10</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Mortgage loan financing and property investment firm DC Finance changed its name from Lucky Man Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>The company proposed a five-for-two shares bonus issue.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted to account for the subdivision of a one-for-two share and capitalisation issue in January 1996.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$77.67 million on disposal of subsidiaries and HK$35.42 million on disposal of associated companies.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is six H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.5 cents) vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
